      "budget_share": 0.7,
      "why": "unrolled_k is the only family I control that has produced feasible points (40 feasible, best luts_plus_ffs 415, 15/19 on the merged front). The spec needs >=1 MSPS throughput and <=2^-10 error. unrolled_k with k=2..4 gives ceil(N/k)+3 cycles/result; with N~10-14 and k=2-4 that is ~5-10 cycles/result, so Fmax must be >=100-200 MHz to hit 1 MSPS. Narrowing data_width to 12-16 and n_iter to 10-14 focuses on the accuracy/area sweet spot: W=12 gives output LSB 2^-10, so n_iter must be high enough that CORDIC residual error stays below 2^-10. angle_guard -2..0 and frac_guard 0..1 keep the datapath narrow to minimize LUTs+FFs while still meeting the error bound. k=2..4 balances throughput (need enough rotations/cycle) against area (more parallel shift/add chains). This is where the trade-off curve lives for my assigned families."
    },
    {
      "family": "iterative",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 16
        ,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
